Standalone gate fix, split out of the tool-gap feature commit per
coordinator directive (supersedes the unmerged a613f36bc7, which carried
it as a rider).

Origin: run from a session worktree, `_repo_relative` could never strip
another checkout's absolute provenance prefix, so `_sha256_at_head` got
an unresolvable path, `drift_is_pre_existing` fail-closed, and the
pre-existing-debt carve-out (REQ-OPS-FRESHNESS-BACKLOG-1) was
unreachable: three artifacts whose every drifted dependency was already
drifted at HEAD still blocked a worktree commit — the exact
--no-verify-training failure the module's docstring names.

The fix, hardened by the same-day adversarial review:
- Fallback relativizes via the git toplevel CONTAINING the recorded
  path, gated on a shared root commit with THIS repo (R1: without the
  gate, an unrelated repo with colliding layout flipped a real block to
  backlog — fail-open on a fail-closed gate; the first cut's regression
  test PINNED that bug and was rewritten to assert the opposite).
- Both the toplevel probe AND the block-deciding `_sha256_at_head` strip
  the four git discovery overrides (R2: hooks run with GIT_DIR /
  GIT_INDEX_FILE exported; cwd does not beat GIT_DIR — measured: every
  dependency degraded to its bare basename at hook time, and a poisoned
  head hash returned the impostor repo's blob).
- The strip is the explicit denylist {GIT_DIR, GIT_WORK_TREE,
  GIT_INDEX_FILE, GIT_COMMON_DIR}, not GIT_* wholesale (R3: CI injects
  safe.directory via GIT_CONFIG_*, and stripping GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES
  widens discovery instead of narrowing it).

Unresolvable stays None and the caller keeps blocking: the error
direction is unchanged, fail-closed. Live corpus re-verified after the
relatedness gate: the three backlog artifacts still classify
pre-existing (worktree and main share the root commit) and the full lint
reports OK.

Mutations M15 (fallback reverted), M16 (strip emptied), M25 (relatedness
gate removed), M26 (head-hash env strip removed): each RED, restored
byte-identical. R3's keep-config direction is stated, not
mutation-proven — a dubious-ownership repo cannot be constructed without
root in this environment.

Mutation-gate note: two pending markers armed during this session's own
mutation-driver pytest windows named openspec spec.md, ops/arc_tool_gaps.md,
ops/changelog.md and ops/status.md as [NOT this run] writes. Those are this
session's DELIBERATE append-only doc edits, made concurrently with the
driver's focused test runs; the tests themselves write nothing tracked.
Markers retired deliberately per the gate's own instruction.

